        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Minh Diep",
          "email": "mdiep@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-17 21:14:34.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-17559 build: fix deb repackaging of multiple LNDs",
        "message": "LU-17559 build: fix deb repackaging of multiple LNDs\n\nWith --enable-multiple-lnds, debian/repackage-multiple-lnds.sh\ndoes not split the LNDs into correct lustre-lnet-module-*\npackages:\n\n- it enters debian/tmp/re-pkg/<package>/DEBIAN, which nothing\n  creates, so no LND package is built; create it, starting from an\n  empty debian/tmp/re-pkg.\n- it runs outside fakeroot, so the packages it builds are owned by\n  the building user; pass --root-owner-group to dpkg-deb --build.\n- with only the in-kernel o2iblnd built, ko2iblnd.ko is a symlink\n  that it packages as an empty lustre-lnet-module-o2iblnd; only\n  package a regular file, and drop the symlink once the in-kernel\n  package provides ko2iblnd.ko.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ralph Goff <ralph.goff@netapp.com>\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ibe61bd63b1682f546b5ab7bbf7009dbf023e28f9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
